QuickJS in MintVID
==================

This directory contains the embeddable QuickJS engine from:

  https://github.com/bellard/quickjs

Pinned upstream commit:

  04be246001599f5995fa2f2d8c91a0f198d3f34c

Upstream version file:

  2026-06-04

MintVID builds only the core interpreter. quickjs-libc.c is deliberately not
included, so JavaScript has no filesystem, process, socket or operating-system
bindings. MR_QUICKJS_NO_THREADS disables SharedArrayBuffer/Atomics support;
the YouTube challenge solver does not require it and classic AmigaOS does not
provide pthreads.

MR_QUICKJS_PORTABLE_TIME selects standard-C time fallbacks for the AmigaOS
build, whose C library does not guarantee POSIX gettimeofday(), localtime_r()
or tm_gmtoff. The EJS solver does not depend on sub-second Date/Math.random
seeding.

The unused upstream fenv.h include is omitted because Bebbo's AmigaOS C
library does not provide that header; QuickJS 2026-06-04 makes no fenv calls.

The upstream MIT licence is retained as LICENSE.

For repository-tooling compatibility, the large upstream quickjs.c translation
unit is mechanically divided at top-level function boundaries into three
quickjs_part*.inc files and reassembled by the small quickjs.c wrapper. This
does not create separate translation units or alter the generated program.
